<title>UK: News Corp BSkyB securities issue on track.</title>
<headline>News Corp BSkyB securities issue on track.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rupert Murdoch's News Corp is pressing ahead with plans to sell preferred securities for the purchase of stock in BSkyB, a company spokeswoman said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal is still on track,&quot; a spokeswoman for News Corp's News International UK arm told Reuters.  </p>
<p>News Corp, which has a 40 percent stake in BSkyB, said last week it planned to sell to institutional investors $1 billion of preferred securities to buy BSkyB stock.</p>
<p>There were market rumours earlier on Friday that News Corp was abandoning the plan. The spokeswoman gave no details on how the issue would proceed.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
